# XCU alias
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#
# alias is an intrinsic utility (XCU 1.7), so it is exercised through the
# shell running the test. A definition is put to use with eval, on a line
# after the one that defined it: the standard lets a shell defer a change
# of an alias until the complete command that made it has finished (XCU
# 2.3.1). Names used are unlikely to clash with any predefined alias.

assertion  XCU.alias.001
anchor     utilities/alias.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/alias.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.3.1
class      required
since      1992
says       alias name=string defines the alias and exits zero; the next
           command read that has the name as its command word is
           replaced by the string.
test       t/001-define.sh

assertion  XCU.alias.002
anchor     utilities/alias.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/alias.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       alias with a name operand writes exactly one line that begins
           with the name and an equals sign, then the value quoted, and
           ends with a newline.
test       t/002-show-one.sh

assertion  XCU.alias.003
anchor     utilities/alias.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       The line written for an alias holding quotes, spaces, a dollar
           sign and backslashes is suitable for reinput: after the alias
           is removed, giving the line to alias again restores a
           definition that behaves as before.
test       t/003-reinput.sh

assertion  XCU.alias.004
anchor     utilities/alias.html#OPERANDS
anchor     utilities/alias.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       alias with no operands writes the definition of every alias
           that exists, one name=value line each.
test       t/004-list-all.sh

assertion  XCU.alias.005
anchor     utilities/alias.html#EXIT STATUS
anchor     utilities/alias.html#STDOUT
class      required
since      1992
says       alias with the name of an alias that does not exist exits with
           a status greater than zero and writes nothing to standard
           output.
test       t/005-missing-status.sh

assertion  XCU.alias.006
anchor     utilities/alias.html#EXIT STATUS
anchor     utilities/alias.html#STDERR
anchor     utilities/V3_chap01.html#1.4
class      required
since      1992
says       The failure for a missing alias comes with a diagnostic message
           on standard error.
test       t/006-missing-diagnostic.sh

assertion  XCU.alias.007
anchor     utilities/alias.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       Defining a name again replaces the earlier value: the new
           value is what is shown and what is substituted.
test       t/007-redefine.sh

assertion  XCU.alias.008
anchor     utilities/alias.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.13
class      required
since      1992
says       An alias defined in the shell is in effect in its subshells;
           an alias defined in a subshell does not exist in the shell
           that started it.
test       t/008-subshell.sh

assertion  XCU.alias.009
anchor     utilities/alias.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.3.1
class      required
since      1992
says       Alias definitions are not inherited by a separate invocation of
           the shell run from the shell that holds them.
test       t/009-not-inherited.sh

assertion  XCU.alias.010
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.3.1
anchor     utilities/alias.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       When an alias value ends in a blank the word after the
           substituted text is also checked for alias substitution; when
           the value does not end in a blank it is not.
test       t/010-trailing-blank.sh

assertion  XCU.alias.011
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.3.1
anchor     utilities/alias.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       A word containing a quoting character is not subject to alias
           substitution.
test       t/011-quoted.sh

assertion  XCU.alias.012
anchor     utilities/V3_chap02.html#2.3.1
anchor     utilities/alias.html#DESCRIPTION
class      required
since      1992
says       A word that came from the substitution of an alias is not
           substituted again by the same alias, so an alias whose value
           starts with its own name runs that command once.
test       t/012-recursion.sh

assertion  XCU.alias.013
anchor     utilities/alias.html#OPERANDS
class      required
since      1992
says       Several name=string operands in one call each define an alias,
           and several name operands each show a definition.
test       t/013-several.sh
